Dialogue: 0,0:00:02.21,0:00:05.15,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,I will now proceed to break the curse.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:05.57,0:00:07.61,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,I didn't think you'd make it in time.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:07.61,0:00:09.36,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,Analyzing the curse?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:09.36,0:00:11.74,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,Of course I'd make it in time.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:11.74,0:00:13.57,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,You'd be left beyond help otherwise.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:13.96,0:00:16.24,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,Hurry up and go to sleep already.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:16.24,0:00:18.87,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,I can't have you conscious for the procedure.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:24.17,0:00:25.61,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,Half a year, huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:25.61,0:00:26.93,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,It passed by in a flash.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:26.93,0:00:28.02,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,You're still awake!
Dialogue: 0,0:00:28.02,0:00:29.71,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,I can't fall asleep that quickly.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:32.22,0:00:36.67,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,When I first saw you, I thought \Nyou were a woman made for me.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:38.36,0:00:41.47,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,I had no idea why this curse was cast on me,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:41.47,0:00:43.37,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,but I believed it was so I'd meet you.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:44.34,0:00:45.12,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,Yes.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:45.12,0:00:47.52,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,I came here to meet you.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:50.13,0:00:51.36,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,Tinasha.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:51.36,0:00:52.35,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,What is it?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:53.62,0:00:55.07,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,You're really going to break it?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:55.48,0:00:56.62,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,Yes.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:00.11,0:01:01.03,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,Please do.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:38.18,0:02:43.01,Ep Title,Sign,0,0,0,,{\fad(500,1)}~ Returning the Promise ~
Dialogue: 0,0:02:47.17,0:02:51.56,Default,Lazar,0,0,0,,It's hard to believe that \NLady Tinasha's returned home.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:51.94,0:02:54.67,Default,Lazar,0,0,0,,To think we're here for her coronation today.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:55.25,0:02:57.90,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,She'll be inheriting the spirits \Nof Tuldarr as well.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:58.20,0:03:00.43,Default,Guest A,0,0,0,,Showing off the spirits after all this time...
Dialogue: 0,0:03:00.43,0:03:02.35,Default,Guest A,0,0,0,,Could there be an ulterior motive?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:02.35,0:03:03.77,Default,Guest B,0,0,0,,Don't worry.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:03.77,0:03:06.98,Default,Guest B,0,0,0,,She may be inheriting them, \Nbut I doubt she can handle more than one.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:06.98,0:03:09.68,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,{\i1}She already has a spirit serving her...
Dialogue: 0,0:03:28.97,0:03:30.30,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,Appear before me...
Dialogue: 0,0:03:33.93,0:03:37.87,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,spirits that rest in Tuldarr by ancient pact.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:38.52,0:03:42.64,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,I am Tinasha As Meyer Ur Aeterna Tuldarr.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:43.49,0:03:46.62,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,As your ruler, my declaration defines you.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:46.92,0:03:48.11,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,Come to me.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:55.32,0:03:56.25,Default,Lazar,0,0,0,,Look at that!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:01.61,0:04:02.52,Default,Guest A,0,0,0,,That can't be!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:02.52,0:04:04.30,Default,Guest A,0,0,0,,All twelve spirits?!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:05.38,0:04:08.26,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,Heed my command, twelve spirits of Tuldarr.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:08.92,0:04:14.23,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,As your ruler, I declare an end \Nto our ancient, long-lived pact.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:15.17,0:04:19.15,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,You are hereby released \Nfrom your binding chains.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:19.15,0:04:21.20,Default-Top,Tinasha,0,0,0,,This means you are now free.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:19.69,0:04:22.65,White-Standard,Sign,0,0,0,,{\fad(400,400)\pos(448,301)\3a&HA5&\4a&HA2&}Lilia
Dialogue: 0,0:04:21.20,0:04:22.70,Default-Top,Tinasha,0,0,0,,You may do as you wish.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:22.70,0:04:24.70,Default,Calste,0,0,0,,Wh-What?!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:24.70,0:04:29.16,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,Bygone is the era in which a ruler \Nmust wield fearsome power.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:29.72,0:04:33.87,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,Tuldarr is a powerful nation, \Neven without the spirits.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:34.14,0:04:36.37,Default,Calste,0,0,0,,Legis, did you know she would do this?!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:36.37,0:04:37.94,Default,Legis,0,0,0,,Yes, Father.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:37.94,0:04:39.09,Default,Calste,0,0,0,,How absurd!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:39.55,0:04:44.68,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,For the next year, I will be the last queen \Nto succeed our ancient traditions.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:45.61,0:04:48.58,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,Prince Legis will take the throne after me
Dialogue: 0,0:04:48.58,0:04:51.64,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,and rule Tuldarr with\N a new government in place.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:52.58,0:04:54.28,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,There you have it.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:54.28,0:04:56.60,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,Thanks for everything you've done for us.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:56.60,0:04:59.61,White-Standard,Sign,0,0,0,,{\fad(1,400)\3a&HA5&\4a&HA2&\pos(416,302)}Karr
Dialogue: 0,0:04:56.89,0:04:58.80,Default-Top,Karr,0,0,0,,We can really do whatever we want?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:58.80,0:05:00.19,Default-Top,Tinasha,0,0,0,,Of course.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:00.92,0:05:04.57,Default,Karr,0,0,0,,Then I'll take this chance to serve you \Nas a spirit until you die, little girl.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:05.16,0:05:08.07,Default,Karr,0,0,0,,I'm still free to consider you my queen.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:08.42,0:05:11.04,Default,Mila,0,0,0,,Lady Tinasha, I'll stay with you as well!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:11.04,0:05:13.71,Default-Top,Nil,0,0,0,,Huh? Maybe I should stay, too.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:11.04,0:05:14.04,White-Standard,Sign,0,0,0,,{\fad(1,400)\3a&HA5&\4a&HA2&\pos(320,302)}Nil
Dialogue: 0,0:05:13.71,0:05:15.74,Default-Top,Nil,0,0,0,,I know I won't be bored \Nwith Her Majesty around.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:15.74,0:05:17.00,Default,Mila,0,0,0,,Feel free to leave, Nil!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:17.00,0:05:18.09,Default,Mila,0,0,0,,You're in the way!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:18.49,0:05:20.53,Default,Legis,0,0,0,,They're quite fond of you.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:20.53,0:05:24.72,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,I'd say it's more like \Nthey enjoy messing with me.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:24.72,0:05:27.72,White-Standard,Sign,0,0,0,,{\fad(1,400)\3a&HA5&\4a&HA2&\pos(320,302)}Itz
Dialogue: 0,0:05:25.09,0:05:30.02,Default-Top,Itz,0,0,0,,I thank you for declaring an end to our pact.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:30.02,0:05:35.06,Default,Itz,0,0,0,,But, as Karr suggests, please allow us \Nto stay with you until the end.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:35.06,0:05:38.69,Default,Itz,0,0,0,,We choose to obey you of our own free will.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:38.69,0:05:41.77,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,Well, I did say you could do as you wish.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:42.22,0:05:44.65,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,Please stay with me for the time being, then.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:44.65,0:05:47.00,Default,Itz,0,0,0,,It would be our pleasure.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:59.03,0:06:01.90,Default,Doan,0,0,0,,I don't think anyone expected her to do that.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:02.21,0:06:04.74,Default,Doan,0,0,0,,I suppose even with Queen Tinasha's bloodline,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:04.74,0:06:08.62,Default,Doan,0,0,0,,there would still have come a time \Nwhen the spirits could no longer be inherited.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:08.62,0:06:11.82,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,That said, as long as the spirits \Nremain while she's in power,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:11.82,0:06:14.43,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,that's enough to deter foreign intervention.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:14.70,0:06:18.49,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,The question is whether they can establish \Na new government in that time.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:21.54,0:06:22.48,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,Where's Tinasha?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:22.48,0:06:24.44,Default,Legis,0,0,0,,She's fighting with my father.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:24.44,0:06:26.35,Default,Legis,0,0,0,,I imagine it won't be much longer.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:29.53,0:06:31.95,Default,Legis,0,0,0,,King Oscar. Do you have a moment?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:37.18,0:06:38.36,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,There she is.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:46.76,0:06:49.07,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,Y-You again?!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:49.07,0:06:50.55,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,What do you mean, "again?"
Dialogue: 0,0:06:51.95,0:06:53.76,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,Never mind.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:54.34,0:06:56.76,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,There should be a barrier up.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:56.76,0:06:58.73,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,I easily managed my way in.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:59.01,0:07:00.28,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,How insecure.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:00.28,0:07:03.69,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,Not many people can break my barrier.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:04.05,0:07:06.38,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,That was quite a bold move back there.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:06.38,0:07:09.75,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,Well, I'd made my decision a while back.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:10.57,0:07:12.37,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,What will you do after you step down?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:12.37,0:07:15.61,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,I think it'd be best if I married Legis.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:16.12,0:07:18.87,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,I'm sure Calste would be relieved as well.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:19.34,0:07:21.33,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,Why don't you come with me instead?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:21.33,0:07:22.42,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,What?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:23.29,0:07:26.00,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,In other words, be my wife.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:26.66,0:07:28.85,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,I don't think it's a bad deal.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:28.85,0:07:33.55,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,With a new government, it'd be safer \Nto form an alliance with another nation.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:33.55,0:07:36.33,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,Some may see you as a danger,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:36.33,0:07:39.84,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,but they wouldn't dare to take on \Nboth Tuldarr and Farsas.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:40.92,0:07:44.48,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,M-Maybe you're right, but hold on!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:44.99,0:07:48.47,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,No, that was cowardly of me.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:49.08,0:07:50.44,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,Let me start over.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:51.81,0:07:53.24,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,I want you.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:53.70,0:07:55.70,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,That's why I want your hand in marriage.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:56.29,0:07:57.41,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,Nothing more.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:58.98,0:08:00.54,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,Well, you still have a year left.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:00.54,0:08:02.28,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,Take some time to think about it.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:02.28,0:08:04.63,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,W-Wait a minute!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:04.63,0:08:06.49,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,Why the window?!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:06.49,0:08:08.34,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,Wait, no!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:08.66,0:08:11.74,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,I thought you weren't interested in me!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:11.74,0:08:14.30,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,My kingdom comes before my personal emotions.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:14.62,0:08:16.90,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,That is why I tried my best \Nnot to grow attached to you.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:17.89,0:08:21.02,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,But that all changes if you're \Ngoing to abdicate the throne.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:21.37,0:08:23.54,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,I want you by my side.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:23.54,0:08:25.35,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,I don't want anyone else to have you.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:26.30,0:08:28.12,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,If you want me, I'm yours.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:30.79,0:08:31.75,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,Until next time.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:37.41,0:08:41.00,Flashback,Legis,0,0,0,,She is Tuldarr's greatest treasure.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:41.00,0:08:42.83,Flashback,Legis,0,0,0,,Will you offer us what she's worth?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:43.28,0:08:45.71,Flashback,Oscar,0,0,0,,If that's what she wants, then sure.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:48.82,0:08:51.00,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,What is it like in the future you've seen?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:51.74,0:08:54.17,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,Did she end up marrying me?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:59.97,0:09:01.39,Default,Lilia,0,0,0,,Lady Tinasha.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:01.39,0:09:04.64,Default,Lilia,0,0,0,,You need to train to separate \Nyour emotions from your magic.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:04.64,0:09:06.97,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,I did... a long time ago.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:06.97,0:09:08.57,Default,Lilia,0,0,0,,It didn't stick.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:08.57,0:09:09.86,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,Yes...
Dialogue: 0,0:09:09.86,0:09:12.32,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,Next time, I'll use a steel cup.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:12.32,0:09:14.41,Default,Lilia,0,0,0,,Why not deal with the source?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:14.41,0:09:15.73,Default,Lilia,0,0,0,,Like eliminating him.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:15.73,0:09:17.03,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,Not happening!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:17.03,0:09:19.77,Default,Lilia,0,0,0,,I don't know why you're hesitating.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:19.77,0:09:21.99,Default,Lilia,0,0,0,,You came here to meet him \Nin the first place, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:22.28,0:09:24.30,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,That's true...
Dialogue: 0,0:09:24.30,0:09:26.96,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,But this isn't what things were like before.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:27.88,0:09:30.55,Flashback,Oscar,0,0,0,,You'll come and find me for sure.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:31.54,0:09:32.97,Flashback,Oscar,0,0,0,,You'll find happiness.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:33.86,0:09:37.08,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,{\i1}It was the old him that said that.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:37.08,0:09:40.72,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,{\i1}Still, he realized why I came here.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:40.72,0:09:43.14,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,{\i1}And told me not to feel sorry...
Dialogue: 0,0:09:44.03,0:09:46.14,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,I was really happy to hear that.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:46.54,0:09:48.88,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,I was glad I came to this era.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:49.51,0:09:51.34,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,But marrying him?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:51.34,0:09:52.75,Default,Lilia,0,0,0,,What's wrong with that?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:53.40,0:09:56.26,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,I'm not sure why he chose me.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:56.26,0:10:00.24,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,Not to mention, he doesn't know \Nwhat it was like back in the Dark Age.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:00.24,0:10:01.74,Default,Lilia,0,0,0,,That's true.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:01.74,0:10:06.85,Default,Lilia,0,0,0,,Back then, betraying others \Nwas practically a part of growing up.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:06.85,0:10:08.33,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,Was it that bad?!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:08.33,0:10:10.67,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,I mean, I guess it was...
Dialogue: 0,0:10:10.67,0:10:15.71,Default,Lilia,0,0,0,,So perhaps Akashia's wielder actually \Nplans on betraying you as well.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:15.71,0:10:18.98,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,You mean to take me as a hostage for Tuldarr?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:18.98,0:10:21.43,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,That'd be nice and easy to understand.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:21.43,0:10:22.98,Default,Lilia,0,0,0,,So should I eliminate him?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:22.98,0:10:24.42,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,I said "no!"
Dialogue: 0,0:10:25.83,0:10:29.10,Default,Lilia,0,0,0,,I'm glad you seem to be enjoying yourself.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:29.49,0:10:33.70,Default,Lilia,0,0,0,,When you suggested traveling through time, \NI thought you'd finally lost your mind.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:33.70,0:10:36.11,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,That's how little faith you had in me?!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:38.86,0:10:42.87,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,Lilia, how do you think he was able \Nto travel back in time?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:42.87,0:10:45.81,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,It defies the laws of magic.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:45.81,0:10:47.21,Default,Lilia,0,0,0,,I couldn't say.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:47.70,0:10:51.83,Default,Lilia,0,0,0,,Maybe it just looks like he traveled back \Nin time, and it's something else entirely.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:52.28,0:10:55.80,Default,Lilia,0,0,0,,It's human folly to try \Nand understand everything.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:56.26,0:11:00.05,Default,Lilia,0,0,0,,Even our kind cannot \Nperceive many other realms.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:00.05,0:11:03.76,Default,Lilia,0,0,0,,That's why strange phenomena with \Nno explanation occur from time to time.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:04.25,0:11:08.52,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,There were some weird happenings \Nduring my previous reign.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:08.52,0:11:10.23,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,Like the Harvesting.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:10.23,0:11:12.72,Default,Lilia,0,0,0,,Oh, those mysterious ruins.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:16.02,0:11:19.24,Default,Valt,0,0,0,,You should get some sunlight \Nnow and then for your health.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:20.37,0:11:22.08,Default,Miralys,0,0,0,,I don't like the sun.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:23.55,0:11:26.28,Default,Miralys,0,0,0,,I heard the witch took the throne.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:26.28,0:11:27.30,Default,Valt,0,0,0,,It'll be fine.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:27.79,0:11:29.50,Default,Miralys,0,0,0,,What about Farsas?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:29.50,0:11:33.25,Default,Valt,0,0,0,,Akashia is the one uncertain factor, \Nbut it doesn't matter.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:33.56,0:11:37.15,Default,Valt,0,0,0,,We can split the two up and take on the witch.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:37.15,0:11:39.04,Default,Valt,0,0,0,,She's the weaker one.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:39.04,0:11:40.30,Default,Miralys,0,0,0,,Really?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:40.30,0:11:41.88,Default,Valt,0,0,0,,Mentally, that is.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:41.88,0:11:43.83,Default,Valt,0,0,0,,And that's the important part.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:44.22,0:11:48.85,Default,Valt,0,0,0,,When the world is altered, \Nit converges back near its original state,
Dialogue: 0,0:11:48.85,0:11:51.06,Default,Valt,0,0,0,,but it can't fully revert back.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:51.63,0:11:53.78,Default,Valt,0,0,0,,So the world is waiting for an opportunity.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:53.78,0:11:56.08,Default,Valt,0,0,0,,One push to bring it back \Nto its original state.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:59.21,0:12:01.66,Default,Miralys,0,0,0,,I don't want you to die.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:04.71,0:12:05.94,Default,Valt,0,0,0,,It'll be fine.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:08.34,0:12:11.25,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,The ruins unearthed in the southwest?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:11.70,0:12:13.71,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,Didn't we send out an expedition?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:14.75,0:12:16.42,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,None of them have returned?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:16.42,0:12:20.22,Default,Kumu,0,0,0,,All the residents of the villages \Nnear the ruins have gone missing, too.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:20.22,0:12:24.38,Default,Kumu,0,0,0,,Also, the entrance to the ruins are enchanted \Nwith a spell to prevent deterioration,
Dialogue: 0,0:12:24.83,0:12:29.73,Default,Kumu,0,0,0,,but its composition uses techniques \Nunseen in known magical history.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:29.73,0:12:32.78,Default,Kumu,0,0,0,,Therefore, I believe we should seal off the ruins.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:35.81,0:12:37.74,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,Just as you hoped for...
Dialogue: 0,0:12:37.74,0:12:39.56,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,Or perhaps feared?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:39.56,0:12:40.83,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,I'll go check it out.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:44.24,0:12:47.24,White-Standard,Sign,0,0,0,,{\fad(1,500)}Outsider Ruins    {\fs14}Southwestern Farsas
Dialogue: 0,0:12:44.97,0:12:47.30,Default-Top,Oscar,0,0,0,,If anything happens, \Nfeel free to retreat.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:47.30,0:12:49.05,Default-Top,Oscar,0,0,0,,Make safety your first priority.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:49.05,0:12:49.84,Default-Top,Group,0,0,0,,Yes!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:54.12,0:12:56.12,Default,Doan,0,0,0,,It's too pristine.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:56.12,0:12:57.84,Default,Doan,0,0,0,,The walls are seamless.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:57.84,0:12:59.57,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,We're pretty deep inside now.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:59.57,0:13:00.65,Default,Doan,0,0,0,,Yes.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:00.65,0:13:04.56,Default,Doan,0,0,0,,You'd expect to pass through the mountain \Nand reach the surface by now.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:05.25,0:13:06.27,Default,Soldier,0,0,0,,Your Majesty!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:06.68,0:13:09.14,Default,Soldier,0,0,0,,General Granfort has gone missing!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:09.14,0:13:10.03,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,What?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:10.03,0:13:11.85,Default,Soldier,0,0,0,,I can't find the other soldiers, either!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:12.26,0:13:14.10,Default,Doan,0,0,0,,We already have people missing?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:14.10,0:13:16.31,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,I didn't sense anything out of the ordinary.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:16.31,0:13:18.02,Default,Doan,0,0,0,,What's going on here?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:18.46,0:13:19.23,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,Step back!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:22.94,0:13:23.65,Default,Doan,0,0,0,,Your Majesty!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:34.20,0:13:35.51,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,That's not good.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:36.00,0:13:37.55,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,We're all split up now.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:48.01,0:13:49.14,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,What?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:54.83,0:13:56.10,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,What in the world?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:56.50,0:13:58.89,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,Are these ruins full of ghosts?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:05.97,0:14:08.52,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,Are you... Tinasha?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:19.62,0:14:21.21,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,Thanks, Nark!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:26.60,0:14:29.22,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,How sickening.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:29.22,0:14:30.65,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,This will give me nightmares.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:37.46,0:14:38.81,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,Oscar?!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:40.60,0:14:42.01,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,Oscar, wait!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:45.45,0:14:47.29,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,It sure is a good resemblance.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:47.29,0:14:49.40,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,Wait! Y-You're too close!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:49.78,0:14:51.86,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,The more I look, the more you resemble her.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:51.86,0:14:53.37,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,It's the real me!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:54.51,0:14:56.83,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,W-Wait, I'm really...
Dialogue: 0,0:15:01.67,0:15:04.13,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,So? How'd you come here?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:04.13,0:15:06.08,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,You knew all along?!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:06.08,0:15:07.33,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,Of course I did.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:07.33,0:15:08.74,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,Just a bit of banter.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:10.95,0:15:14.89,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,A magical attack made contact \Nwith the barrier I placed on you,
Dialogue: 0,0:15:14.89,0:15:17.35,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,so I went to Farsas to see what happened.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:17.88,0:15:20.35,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,Als told me everything, so I came here.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:20.35,0:15:21.82,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,So that was it.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:22.26,0:15:24.21,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,Did you fight a mage?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:24.21,0:15:25.09,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,Yeah.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:25.09,0:15:27.05,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,You, but slightly younger.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:27.05,0:15:28.00,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,Huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:28.00,0:15:31.14,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,So it got a record of me after all?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:31.14,0:15:32.10,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,A record?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:32.54,0:15:36.87,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,This place is sort of a repository \Nto preserve records of humans.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:37.14,0:15:42.83,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,I don't understand the mechanics, but it \Ncaptures humans to create copies of them.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:43.65,0:15:48.38,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,The copies it creates \Nare stored as simple data,
Dialogue: 0,0:15:48.38,0:15:53.30,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,but they can also materialize \Nto get rid of any detected intruders.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:53.30,0:15:55.47,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,So that's what I faced.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:55.47,0:15:59.27,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,Tuldarr records refer to it as the Harvesting.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:59.70,0:16:04.15,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,I came here four hundred years ago, \Nand I found myself captured.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:04.15,0:16:05.96,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,I managed to escape halfway through,
Dialogue: 0,0:16:05.96,0:16:08.86,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,but I guess it got enough data \Nto materialize me.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:08.86,0:16:11.16,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,That's an ominous name.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:11.16,0:16:12.86,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,What happens to those it captures?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:14.55,0:16:16.06,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,Duplication chambers.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:16.69,0:16:18.81,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,They should be sleeping here.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:20.58,0:16:23.00,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,I'll open a teleportation \Nportal at the entrance,
Dialogue: 0,0:16:23.00,0:16:25.90,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,so go wake the people inside.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:25.90,0:16:28.88,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,They're encased in cocoons, \Nbut it's safe to cut them free.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:29.43,0:16:33.59,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,A large number of guardians will spawn, \Nbut I'll take care of them.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:33.59,0:16:35.47,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,Will you be okay on your own?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:35.47,0:16:36.94,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,I'll be fine.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:36.94,0:16:40.31,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,But I might not be able to last long, \Nso please hurry.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:40.59,0:16:42.28,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,Call me if things look bad.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:42.28,0:16:43.52,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,Don't get hurt.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:44.13,0:16:45.71,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,I'll keep that in mind.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:53.61,0:16:54.80,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,Go on.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:54.80,0:16:55.71,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,Yeah.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:56.97,0:17:00.08,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,Steel unformed into blade, \Ndefined by my words.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:00.08,0:17:01.33,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,Rift of negation.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:01.33,0:17:03.39,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,Time unbound to pain.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:06.70,0:17:07.71,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,Reject them.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:12.25,0:17:13.67,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,Doan. Wake up!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:18.14,0:17:20.05,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,There's a teleportation portal at the entrance.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:20.05,0:17:22.32,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,Destroy the cocoons \Nand evacuate the people inside.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:22.32,0:17:24.35,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,If you find palace soldiers, have them help!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:24.97,0:17:27.10,Default,Doan,0,0,0,,At your command...
Dialogue: 0,0:17:30.05,0:17:31.09,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,Karr! Senn!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:31.09,0:17:31.65,Default,Karr,0,0,0,,Yeah, yeah.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:31.65,0:17:32.44,Default,Senn,0,0,0,,You called?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:32.89,0:17:34.24,Default,Karr,0,0,0,,This place again?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:34.24,0:17:35.45,Default,Karr,0,0,0,,I hate it here.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:35.45,0:17:37.95,White-Standard,Sign,0,0,0,,{\fad(1,500)\3a&HA5&\4a&HA2&\pos(307,302)}Senn
Dialogue: 0,0:17:35.72,0:17:38.03,Default-Top,Senn,0,0,0,,Stop complaining and get to work, Karr.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:55.44,0:17:57.09,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,Can you keep going a little longer?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:58.27,0:18:00.30,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,I'm fine. I can do it.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:01.05,0:18:02.18,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,Tinasha!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:02.90,0:18:05.26,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,The enemy's begun to interfere.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:05.26,0:18:07.81,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,They're trying to close the portal by force.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:07.81,0:18:08.77,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,What?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:08.77,0:18:10.73,Default,Senn,0,0,0,,For crying out loud...
Dialogue: 0,0:18:11.26,0:18:13.19,Default,Karr,0,0,0,,There's no end to them.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:17.16,0:18:19.62,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,Tinasha, lend me your vision.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:19.62,0:18:20.57,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,What?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:24.89,0:18:26.51,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,Please be careful.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:28.99,0:18:30.46,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,I'll be fine.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:45.01,0:18:46.12,Default,Senn,0,0,0,,Oh.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:46.12,0:18:47.23,Default,Karr,0,0,0,,He's pretty good!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:54.57,0:18:55.65,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,This is it.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:10.40,0:19:11.55,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,The core...
Dialogue: 0,0:19:14.76,0:19:16.85,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,Why are you laughing?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:16.85,0:19:18.46,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,You're making a funny face.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:18.78,0:19:20.01,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,Is now the time?!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:20.44,0:19:22.30,Default,Voice,0,0,0,,Damn you, insider...
Dialogue: 0,0:19:26.78,0:19:27.71,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,What was that?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:28.18,0:19:29.46,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,Was I hearing things?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:32.83,0:19:36.19,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,What in the world created those ruins?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:36.51,0:19:40.06,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,I'd like to know, but I don't have \Nthe slightest clue.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:40.48,0:19:43.07,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,It operates on forces \Noutside the laws of magic,
Dialogue: 0,0:19:43.07,0:19:45.16,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,so there's nothing to go off of.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:45.99,0:19:50.60,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,Even on other planes of existence, \Nthere are no laws that defy the laws of magic.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:50.60,0:19:54.17,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,That would mean going against this very world.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:54.76,0:19:57.04,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,What about outside this world?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:57.04,0:19:59.29,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,What? Outside this world?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:59.87,0:20:03.33,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,There's no way to prove that even exists.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:03.33,0:20:04.59,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,It's impossible.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:08.66,0:20:11.02,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,You have plenty of time \Nto answer my engagement offer.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:11.36,0:20:12.74,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,We still have a year left.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:14.29,0:20:16.46,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,Have you received any other \Nproposals since then?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:16.86,0:20:18.73,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,From seven countries or so.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:19.10,0:20:20.10,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,Oh?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:20.44,0:20:22.42,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,Don't give me that look!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:22.42,0:20:25.20,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,They're proposing just because \Nthey want a magical weapon!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:25.20,0:20:26.32,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,Are you sure?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:26.89,0:20:29.55,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,What do you even see in me?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:29.55,0:20:30.90,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,You're weird.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:30.90,0:20:32.66,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,What does {\i1}that{\i0} mean?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:32.66,0:20:35.49,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,You don't know anything about me.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:35.49,0:20:39.59,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,In the Dark Age, they used \Nto call me the Ice Queen...
Dialogue: 0,0:20:42.45,0:20:46.61,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,You'd regret spending\N your life with me if you knew.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:46.61,0:20:47.64,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,Really?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:50.61,0:20:52.64,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,If you want to tell me, then tell me.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:52.64,0:20:54.76,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,If you want to hide it, then hide it.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:55.16,0:20:57.45,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,I could know everything, \Nand I'd still feel the same.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:58.25,0:21:02.99,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,I did my best to make sure \Nyou'd expect nothing from me.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:06.09,0:21:08.41,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,You're fine if you end up regretting it?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:09.06,0:21:10.01,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,Yeah.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:10.01,0:21:12.00,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,I want to spend my life with you.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:12.56,0:21:17.33,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,Let me indulge my personal \Nemotions for once in my life.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:24.37,0:21:26.91,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,I understand what you're \Ntrying to say very well.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:27.41,0:21:31.44,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,I'd rather not keep you waiting, \Nso here's my answer.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:33.08,0:21:34.84,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,Thank you for the kind offer.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:35.41,0:21:39.05,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,If you'll have me, I'll gladly accept.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:53.82,0:21:55.30,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,You're too close.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:56.67,0:21:57.70,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,Get used to it.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:35.47,0:23:40.02,Next Ep Title,Sign,0,0,0,,{\fad(500,1)}~ Bloodless Scars ~
